  "notes": {
    "heritage": "The EA71 established Subaru's reputation for building practical, capable vehicles. The combination of the flat-four engine with the part-time 4WD system created a niche that Subaru would dominate for decades.",
    "iconic_vehicles": "The BRAT became a cult classic in the USA. Its jump seats in the bed (to classify as a passenger vehicle and avoid the 'Chicken Tax' on imported trucks) became legendary.",
    "4wd_system": "The part-time 4WD system used a simple transfer case with 2WD/4WD lever selection. Not designed for dry pavement 4WD operation.",
